  "summary": "Eduard served as Managing Partner and Chief Investment Officer of Montana Capital Partners, where he was a member of the Executive Committee and the Investment Committee, while also overseeing the investment activities in the U.S. and focusing particularly on GP-led continuation vehicle (CV) transactions.\n\nEduard previously was with AlpInvest Partners, the private equity fund-of-funds and secondaries arm of The Carlyle Group, where he led the firm’s portfolio management activities. \n\nPrior to that, he led the New York office of Swiss Re Private Equity Partners, the private markets fund-of-funds business of Swiss Re (acquired by BlackRock). Eduard started his career in both Munich and New York at Allianz Capital Partners, one of the largest Europe-based institutional investors in private equity funds, with further experience gained at HgCapital in London, a leading European private equity firm.\n\nEduard has a degree in business and economics from Ludwig-Maximilian University of Munich and an MBA with honors from the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania.",
